🐛 Describe the bug
The initDeviceStreamState() can only be called by calling getStreamFromPool(). And if user calls APIs like getCurrentOpenRegStream() or getDefaultOpenRegStream(), then something will failed.



      pytorch/test/cpp_extensions/open_registration_extension/torch_openreg/csrc/runtime/OpenRegStream.cpp


        Lines 200 to 212
      in
      c297b02







           OpenRegStream getStreamFromPool(const int priority, DeviceIndex device_index) { 




             initOpenRegStreamsOnce(); 




             if (device_index == -1) { 




               device_index = current_device(); 




             } 




             c10::call_once( 




                 device_flags[device_index], initDeviceStreamState, device_index); 




             auto pri_idx = 




                 std::clamp(priority, 0, max_compile_time_stream_priorities - 1); 




             const auto idx = get_idx(priority_counters[device_index][pri_idx]); 




             auto id_type = static_cast<StreamIdType>(pri_idx); 




             return OpenRegStreamForId(device_index, makeStreamId(id_type, idx)); 




           } 





Common used APIs won't initiate device stream state:



      pytorch/test/cpp_extensions/open_registration_extension/torch_openreg/csrc/runtime/OpenRegStream.cpp


